      "value": "Example avatar IDs:\n\n- Katz Manuka (avtr_1404c040-f29d-4b5d-8aa6-0fcb1273edb6) - public\n\n- Comfy ManukaFT Hush_Rush (avtr_bbc3408e-d7c1-497d-88c4-5ac7731d7655) - private\n\n- Comfy MoeFT Hush_Rush (Preview) (avtr_5d925964-e921-4b24-81a9-f19eef7d3eb1) - private\n\nTo clarify OP's post: This isn't an armature / FBX export settings scale or mismatching issue, it's caused by applying an animation to the avatar 3D preview (and may be intended behavior, fixed maximum width). Without the animation, the avatar size in the preview is taller and perfectly as expected.",
